Small dry run: in `[[1, 0, 3], [4, 5, 6]]`, the marker arrays become `zeroRows = [true, false]` and `zeroColumns = [false, true, false]`. The first row and middle column are then cleared.

Time complexity: `O(m * n)`. Space complexity: `O(m + n)`. The matrix is modified directly, while the two marker arrays hold the extra information.

The first row and first column can store the row and column marks, so no row arrays are needed. Two flags protect the original state of those special borders. Without the flags, a zero in the top row or left column could be lost among the markers.

The inner cells are processed only after all marks have been recorded. The border is handled last.

